From 15459e0520e0f914513cf060dc991ea9d38f4f0d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gemini experiment archive <experiment@invalid.example>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 22:37:27 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wlan: observe native AHB DMA lifetimes

Join HIF initialization ordinals to full DMA API addresses, actual PDMA
programming arguments, read-preserving poll summaries and unmap boundaries.
Keep transaction state within the native HIF critical section. Atomically
retire identity at HIF cleanup without acquiring a possibly retained HIF
lock, and report a failed capture before an explicit native DMA reset.

Use the built-in capture owner's existing activity and append interfaces.
Failed recording does not repair, retry or alter the native hardware path.
Preserve the selected deadline return with its outstanding mapping and
lock, and the independent idle-count escape followed by unmap.

This unselected native 3.18 experiment depends on the pstore capture series
through patch 10. It supplies no controller, watchdog, candidate, resource
admission or hardware evidence. The synthetic archive identity does not
certify authorship; this patch is not submission-ready.
